---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="WiFi and WAP options | OurPort" description="Review Ethernet, existing property WiFi and optional WAP approaches for an OurPort laundry locker site.">
  <section class="container option-hero">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Optional site extension · WiFi & WAP</p><h1>Connect the locker <span>on purpose.</span></h1><p class="lead">Ethernet is the preferred working path. An existing property WAP may be suitable after a site and RF review; an added access point is a coordinated option where the property needs it.</p><a class="button" href="/plan-a-site/?role=housing">Discuss your network path <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <figure class="diagram-hero"><img src="/images/wifi-wap-distribution-concept.jpg" width="1600" height="537" alt="Concept floor plan showing a central OurPort locker node connected to WiFi access-point and camera endpoints in east and west residence halls." fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption><span>Residence-hall endpoint study</span><span>Illustrative concept · not a site design</span></figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <section class="section option-tint option-tint-warm"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Connection approaches</p><h2>Start with what the property already supports.</h2></div><p>The final route follows property policy, coverage, security segmentation and field verification.</p></div><div class="option-paths"><article><span>Preferred</span><h3>Dedicated Ethernet</h3><p>Coordinate a property-approved wired path and network policy for reliable locker communications.</p></article><article><span>Site survey</span><h3>Existing property WiFi</h3><p>Validate signal, authentication, segmentation and support ownership before relying on the existing WAP.</p></article><article><span>Optional extension</span><h3>Added WAP</h3><p>Consider a property-approved access point when the locker location can also serve an identified coverage need.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section container option-decisions"><div><p class="eyebrow">Network discovery</p><h2>Questions for facilities and IT.</h2></div><ol><li><span>01</span>Is Ethernet available at the proposed wall</li><li><span>02</span>Which network segment may be used</li><li><span>03</span>Is existing WiFi approved for this device</li><li><span>04</span>Who owns the WAP and ongoing support</li><li><span>05</span>Which camera or other PoE endpoints are planned</li><li><span>06</span>What must recover locally during an outage</li></ol></section>
  <section class="section option-diagram"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A coordinated path</p><h2>Separate network, power and ownership.</h2></div><p>The concept keeps property authority visible and treats the WAP, camera and locker controls as individually approved endpoints.</p></div><figure><img src="/images/data-power-governance-flow.png" width="1872" height="1216" alt="Concept diagram showing property LAN, existing WAP, managed PoE, locker controls and optional monitoring paths." loading="lazy" /><figcaption><span>Data, power and governance concept</span><span>For coordination only · engineering validation required</span></figcaption></figure></div></section>
  <section class="container sibling-option"><div><p class="eyebrow">Related option</p><h2>Coordinate camera monitoring.</h2><p>If a camera is considered, define its coverage, network, owner, video platform and retention policy with the property.</p></div><a class="button button-outline" href="/cctv/">Explore CCTV options <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  <CallToAction role="housing" title="Bring facilities and IT into the plan." body="A photo, likely wall and the name of the property’s network contact are enough to begin the site conversation." />
</SiteLayout>
